  "note": "Fourteen Nationalists were nominated for the six seats; Patrick O'Callaghan's paper was declared invalid and seven withdrew under an agreement in the Nationalist ranks (Peter Clarke, John Corrigan senior, John Corrigan junior, John Donaghy, John Hughes, Hugh Knipe and P. M'Kenna), so the remaining six were returned unopposed. O'Reilly and Mullan were retiring members; Thomas M'Laughlin is styled J.P."
